<h1>HRMS Performance Management System — Full Documentation</h1>
<p><strong>System:</strong> Cybaem Tech Enterprise HRMS (Version 2.0)</p>
<p><strong>Module:</strong> Sidebar &rarr; Performance (Goals & KPIs, Appraisals, 360° Feedback, Reports)</p>
<p><strong>Release Cycle:</strong> Q1 2026 Active Implementation</p>
<p><strong>Document Version:</strong> 2.0.0 | <strong>Date:</strong> October 29, 2026</p>

<div class="highlight-box">
  <strong>Executive Summary:</strong><br>
  This document details the corporate quarterly performance management system implemented in the HRMS. The system connects organizational objectives (Goals & KPIs set by HR and Line Managers) with employee self-assessments, manager evaluations (Appraisals), multi-rater 360° feedback, and real-time department analytics and exportable executive reports. All calculations use live database records with zero hardcoded or mock math.
</div>

<h2>1. System Architecture & Performance Flow</h2>
<p>The performance lifecycle is divided into 4 tightly integrated pillars operating on a quarterly cadence (Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4):</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 20%;">Pillar</th>
      <th style="width: 25%;">Primary Stakeholders</th>
      <th style="width: 30%;">Core Capabilities</th>
      <th style="width: 25%;">Output / Downstream Impact</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>1. Goals & KPIs</strong></td>
      <td>HR Admins & Line Managers &rarr; Employees</td>
      <td>Quarterly objectives, KPI target/metric setting, weightage allocation (10-100%), self-progress updates & notes.</td>
      <td>Feeds real-time KPI Achievement Score (%) into quarterly Appraisals.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>2. Appraisals</strong></td>
      <td>Employees &rarr; Department Line Managers &rarr; HR</td>
      <td>KPI-driven scoring, self-assessment (1-5 rating & comments), Line Manager evaluation & feedback, balanced overall score.</td>
      <td>Determines final employee performance ratings, promotions & appraisals.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>3. 360° Feedback</strong></td>
      <td>Managers, Peers, Direct Reports, Cross-functional</td>
      <td>4 Core Competencies (Technical, Delivery, Teamwork, Communication) rated 1-5, qualitative strengths & growth areas.</td>
      <td>Multi-perspective behavioral insights supporting holistic performance evaluation.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>4. Analytics & Reports</strong></td>
      <td>HR Executives & Department HODs</td>
      <td>Department performance ranking, rating distribution bell curves, top performers leaderboard, executive PDF export.</td>
      <td>Strategic talent insights, compensation reviews, and organizational audits.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>2. Module 1: Quarterly Goals & KPIs</h2>
<p>Accessible via <strong>Sidebar &rarr; Performance &rarr; Goals & KPIs</strong>.</p>

<h3>Key Features:</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Quarterly Tabs:</strong> Filter by <code>Q1 (Active)</code>, <code>Q2</code>, <code>Q3</code>, <code>Q4</code>, or <code>All Quarters</code> with year selector (<code>2026</code>).</li>
  <li><strong>Role-Based Creation:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li><span class="badge badge-teal">Set by HR</span>: Organization-wide compliance, code quality, and culture goals set by HR Admins.</li>
      <li><span class="badge badge-blue">Set by Manager</span>: Technical deliverables, architecture milestones, and project execution set by Department Managers.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Add Quarterly Goal Modal:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Department & Assignee Dropdown:</strong> Select department to filter available employees (e.g., Engineering &rarr; Gauri Dhapte, Sujay Palande, Deepa Nair).</li>
      <li><strong>KPI Metric:</strong> Specific measurable target (e.g., <em>"Complete 100% on-time deployment with zero regressions"</em>).</li>
      <li><strong>Target Value vs. Current Value:</strong> Quantifiable measurement (e.g., <em>Target: 100%, Current: 95%</em>).</li>
      <li><strong>Weightage (%):</strong> Objective percentage weight (e.g., 40%, 30%, 30% summing to 100%).</li>
      <li><strong>Priority & Due Date:</strong> High / Medium / Low priority tagging with deadline date picker.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Employee Self-Progress Updating:</strong> Employees click <strong>"Update Progress"</strong> to update completion % slider (0-100%), record their current metric value, write progress notes, and adjust status (<em>On Track, At Risk, Behind, Completed</em>).</li>
  <li><strong>Manager Guidance:</strong> Line Managers can write coaching feedback directly on active goals.</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Module 2: Performance Appraisals</h2>
<p>Accessible via <strong>Sidebar &rarr; Performance &rarr; Appraisals</strong>.</p>

<h3>Automated KPI Achievement Score Calculation:</h3>
<p>The appraisal engine dynamically computes each employee's KPI Achievement Score from their real quarterly goals:</p>

<div class="formula-box">
  <strong>KPI Achievement Score (%)</strong> = &sum; (Goal Progress &times; Goal Weightage) / &sum; (Goal Weightage)<br><br>
  <em>Example for Gauri Dhapte (Q1 2026):</em><br>
  &bull; Goal 1: Leave Workflow Engine (40% wt &times; 95% prog) = 38.0<br>
  &bull; Goal 2: Code Quality & Bug Rate (30% wt &times; 100% prog) = 30.0<br>
  &bull; Goal 3: API Performance Optimization (30% wt &times; 85% prog) = 25.5<br>
  <strong>Total KPI Score = 38.0 + 30.0 + 25.5 = 93.5% &asymp; 94%</strong>
</div>

<h3>Dual Review Workflow:</h3>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Stage 1 — Employee Self-Review:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Employee logs in, sees their computed KPI Score and goal breakdown.</li>
      <li>Provides a Self Rating (1.0 to 5.0) and written accomplishments/highlights.</li>
      <li>Clicks <em>"Submit to Line Manager"</em> &rarr; Status becomes <span class="badge badge-amber">Manager Review</span>.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Stage 2 — Line Manager Evaluation:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Designated Line Manager (e.g., Amit Sharma for Engineering) reviews employee's KPI score and self-evaluation.</li>
      <li>Enters Manager Rating (1.0 to 5.0), verifies KPI achievement, and provides managerial feedback.</li>
      <li>Clicks <em>"Complete Appraisal"</em> &rarr; Status becomes <span class="badge badge-green">Completed</span>.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Stage 3 — Balanced Overall Rating:</strong>
    <div class="formula-box">
      <strong>Overall Rating</strong> = [(KPI Score / 100) &times; 5.0 &times; 0.40] + [Manager Rating &times; 0.60]<br>
      <em>Example: [(94 / 100) &times; 5 &times; 0.4] + [4.7 &times; 0.6] = 1.88 + 2.82 = 4.70 / 5.0</em>
    </div>
  </li>
</ol>

<h2>4. Module 3: 360° Multi-Source Feedback</h2>
<p>Accessible via <strong>Sidebar &rarr; Performance &rarr; 360° Feedback</strong>.</p>

<h3>Evaluation Dimensions & Core Competencies:</h3>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 25%;">Competency Pillar</th>
      <th style="width: 15%;">Scale</th>
      <th style="width: 60%;">Evaluation Focus</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>1. Technical Mastery</strong></td>
      <td>1.0 - 5.0</td>
      <td>Code architecture, technical depth, problem-solving quality, and domain knowledge.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>2. Delivery & Reliability</strong></td>
      <td>1.0 - 5.0</td>
      <td>Meeting sprint deadlines, operational accountability, and deliverable quality.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>3. Teamwork & Culture</strong></td>
      <td>1.0 - 5.0</td>
      <td>Peer support, mentorship, cross-team collaboration, and positive workplace attitude.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>4. Communication & Leadership</strong></td>
      <td>1.0 - 5.0</td>
      <td>Clarity in communication, architectural documentation, and stakeholder alignment.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<p><strong>Reviewer Roles:</strong> Peers, Line Managers, Direct Reports, and Cross-functional collaborators can submit ratings, detailed written strengths, and constructive development areas.</p>

<h2>5. Module 4: Performance Analytics & Department Reports</h2>
<p>Accessible via <strong>Sidebar &rarr; Performance &rarr; Reports</strong>.</p>

<h3>Executive Summary Metrics:</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Department Performance Table:</strong> Compares staff count, active goals, goal delivery percentage, average rating, and top performers across all 11 departments.</li>
  <li><strong>Rating Distribution Bell Curve:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li><em>Exceptional / Outstanding (4.5 - 5.0):</em> Top-tier organizational talent.</li>
      <li><em>Exceeds Expectations (4.0 - 4.4):</em> Strong performers surpassing target KPIs.</li>
      <li><em>Meets Expectations (3.5 - 3.9):</em> Consistent performers delivering on standard expectations.</li>
      <li><em>Needs Development (&lt; 3.5):</em> Employees requiring targeted mentorship and performance plans.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Quarterly High Performers Leaderboard:</strong> Top 5 company-wide performers ranked by cumulative appraisal scores and KPI achievement.</li>
  <li><strong>Executive PDF Export:</strong> Generates formatted reports with department comparison tables, KPI averages, and audit timestamps.</li>
</ul>

